# Library documentation

When implementing against a library **already listed in `package.json`**, fetch current, version-specific docs via Context7 (or the official docs) instead of relying on training data. Prefer the installed major/minor.

Typical stack libraries: React, React Router, Redux Toolkit, Tailwind CSS v4, Ionic React, Capacitor, Vite, Express, Passport, `pg`, Firebase Admin, Stripe, Google Cloud client libs, Testing Library.

Do **not**:

- Add a dependency because Context7 (or any doc source) suggested it
- Change architecture, folder layout, or Tailwind tokens based on generic examples
- Treat Context7 as a source of product UX, schema design, or App Shell patterns

If Context7 is not configured, use official docs or existing code in this repo.
